      <p class="legal-meta">Last updated 8 September 2026</p>

      <p>This page lists the cookies admizz.com actually sets, and what each one is for. It's short because this site keeps cookie use to a minimum — there's no advertising network, no cross-site tracking, and no cookie banner selling your data to anyone.</p>

      <h2>What we use</h2>
      <p>When analytics is enabled on this site, Google Analytics sets a small number of first-party cookies to distinguish visitors and measure usage. These do not identify you by name, and we don't combine them with any other data source to build a profile of you.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Purpose:</strong> understanding which pages are visited, roughly how, and how often, so we can improve the site.</li>
        <li><strong>Set by:</strong> Google Analytics (Google LLC), a third-party analytics provider.</li>
        <li><strong>Duration:</strong> per Google's own default retention settings — see their <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">cookie policy</a> for specifics.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we don't use</h2>
      <p>No advertising or retargeting cookies. No social-media tracking pixels. No cross-site behavioral profiling. The ICEF badge widget in our footer loads a script from ICEF's own servers to display our live accreditation status, but does not set cookies of its own as part of that display.</p>

      <h2>Controlling cookies</h2>
      <p>Most browsers let you block or delete cookies through their settings. Blocking analytics cookies won't affect your ability to use this site — it only means we won't be able to see that your visit happened. You can also opt out of Google Analytics specifically using <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's browser add-on</a>.</p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>See our full <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>, or contact us at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>
    </div>
